  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 1, 'Drink one full glass of water slowly, and let that count as looking after yourself today.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 2, 'Eat a few bites of something simple, like toast, crackers or a piece of fruit, even if you are not hungry.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 3, 'Say the name of the person you lost out loud once today, in a room by yourself or to someone who loved them too.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 4, 'If grief ever brings thoughts of not wanting to live, or feels like too much to carry alone, call or text 988, the Suicide and Crisis Lifeline, any time. Save the number in your phone now.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 5, 'Take a warm shower or wash your face, and let that be enough for this part of the day.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 6, 'Step outside for two minutes and breathe the outdoor air, whatever the weather is doing.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 7, 'When someone offers to help, say yes to one thing, even something small like picking up groceries.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 8, 'Lie down for twenty minutes with your eyes closed, whether or not you sleep.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 9, 'Find one photo of the person you lost and set it somewhere you can see it today.'),
