  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 205, 'Fill a water bottle in the morning and keep it with you through the day.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 206, 'Sort one small pile of their papers today, if you feel ready, and set the rest aside.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 207, 'Sit with your feet flat on the floor and feel your weight supported by the chair.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 208, 'Write a thank you note to someone who cared for the person you lost.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 209, 'Lie on the floor with your legs up on a chair or couch for a few minutes and rest.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 210, 'Tell a friend about one part of your grief they might not see from the outside.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 211, 'Make a playlist of songs that remind you of the person you lost, and play it while you do something ordinary.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 212, 'Write a short prayer, wish or blessing for them, in whatever words feel right.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 213, 'Help a grieving family member with one practical task, like returning a call or running an errand.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 214, 'Bring something of theirs on a walk, like a hat or a small stone, and let it come along.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 215, 'Notice whether you have been forgetting things, and write today''s important tasks on a sticky note.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 216, 'Ask your doctor about your sleep or appetite at your next visit, if they have changed a lot.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 217, 'Eat with someone today, in person or on a video call.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 218, 'Set out a cozy spot for the evening with a blanket, a lamp and a book.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 219, 'Say their name when you talk about them, rather than avoiding it.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 220, 'Describe a decision you are facing in a letter to the person you lost, and imagine their advice.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 221, 'Go outside during a change in the weather, a first frost, a warm breeze or a summer storm, and notice it with them in mind.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 222, 'Ask a friend to come with you to the cemetery, memorial or scattering place, if you want company.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 223, 'Bake something they loved and share it with a neighbor or friend.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 224, 'Remind yourself that if the weight of this loss ever feels like too much to carry alone, or brings thoughts of not wanting to live, you can call or text 988 any time.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 225, 'Light a candle on a hard evening and say a few words to them before you blow it out.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 226, 'Write down what an ordinary day with them looked like, from morning to night.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 227, 'Choose one belonging of theirs to give to someone who would treasure it, when you feel ready.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 228, 'Notice whether grief feels different today than it did before, without judging the change.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 229, 'Ask a coworker to cover one task for you on a day that falls near an anniversary.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 230, 'Plan a quiet way to mark the anniversary of their death, like a walk, a meal or a visit.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 231, 'Let tears come during a movie or song, and let them run their course.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 232, 'Hold a family meal where everyone shares one favorite memory of the person who died.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 233, 'Find one grief support meeting time that would fit your week, and consider trying it once.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 234, 'Rub lotion into your hands slowly, and notice the care in that small act.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 235, 'List a few things you have done since the loss that took courage, however small.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 236, 'Tell a friend which holiday traditions you want to keep, change or skip this year.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 237, 'Visit their favorite restaurant or order their usual dish, and raise a glass to them.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 238, 'Make a donation of time or a few dollars to a cause they cared about.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 239, 'Set a gentle reminder on your phone to drink water in the afternoon.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 240, 'Write down what the person you lost would say to you right now if they could see how you are doing.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 241, 'Spend a few minutes in a garden, park or yard, and notice what is growing or resting.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 242, 'Tell a child that it is okay to feel sad, mad, confused or happy after someone dies.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 243, 'Let a friend take care of one meal this week, start to finish.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 244, 'Make a list of what helps on hard nights, and tape it inside a kitchen cabinet.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 245, 'Notice how you are carrying your head and neck, and roll your shoulders back gently.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 246, 'Ask someone who knew them to write down a memory you can keep.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 247, 'Wear a color they liked today, as a quiet way of carrying them with you.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 248, 'Go to bed with a warm drink and a calm show or audiobook instead of the news.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 249, 'Send a message to a friend who has been quiet lately, and let them know they can still reach out to you.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 250, 'Put on paper, as if writing to them, how the seasons have changed since they died.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 251, 'Give yourself credit for getting through a hard date, whatever that looked like.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 252, 'Find a song that captures how you feel today, and listen to it with your eyes closed.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 253, 'Ask a family member if they would like to share a ritual with you, like a yearly walk or meal.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 254, 'Write down one thing about them that you would like more people to know.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 255, 'Set aside a few minutes to sit in silence and simply think of them.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 256, 'Say yes when someone offers to sit with you at an event or service.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 257, 'Take a walk at a slower pace than usual, and let your breath set the rhythm.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 258, 'Notice whether you are pushing through when you need to rest, and choose rest this once.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 259, 'Tape a note on the fridge with the three things that matter most this week, and let the rest go.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 260, 'If anger is part of your grief, write to the person you lost about a time they frustrated you.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 261, 'Look at their handwriting and trace a letter or word with your finger.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 262, 'Tell someone you trust which reminders of your loss are hardest to see, so they can be gentle around them.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 263, 'Prepare a simple plan for a birthday or holiday: who you will see, where you will go and when you can leave.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 264, 'Spend time with someone who lets you talk about the person you lost without changing the subject.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 265, 'Ask a counselor or a support group about ways to help a grieving child, if one is in your care.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 266, 'Make up a story with a child about something funny the person who died once did.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 267, 'Notice whether you are drinking enough water today, and refill your glass.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 268, 'Let yourself enjoy a good meal without feeling you have to earn it.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 269, 'Keep a list of memories as they come to you, and add one today.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 270, 'Write a few lines about the funeral or memorial, and what you want to remember from it.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 271, 'Open the curtains in the morning and let daylight into the room.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 272, 'Make a phone call you have been putting off, with a friend beside you if that helps.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 273, 'Answer "How are you holding up?" with whatever is true, even if it is "I don''t know."'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 274, 'Look back over this challenge so far and notice one step that felt kind to you.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 275, 'Let someone else carry part of the planning for a memorial, gathering or headstone.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 276, 'Rest your forehead on your palm or a cool surface for a moment and let your face soften.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 277, 'Spend part of the afternoon outside, even on a porch or balcony, and feel the air temperature.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 278, 'Think about how the person you lost liked to celebrate, and borrow one detail for an upcoming occasion.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 279, 'Write down one new thing you have learned to do since they died.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 280, 'Ask a friend to watch a movie with you that you once watched together with the person you lost.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 281, 'Hang a wind chime, bird feeder or plant somewhere you will see it, in their honor.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 282, 'Notice how grief shows up in your stomach or chest, and place a warm hand there.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 283, 'Read a few pages of a book they loved, and see the world for a moment the way they did.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 284, 'Ask someone to help with yard work, cleaning or a repair that the person you lost used to handle.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 285, 'Name one feeling that surprised you this week, and let it be part of grieving.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 286, 'Make a simple rhythm for your evening, like dinner, a shower and bed, so you do not have to decide.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 287, 'Pick a small object, like a stone or a button, to keep in your pocket for comfort.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 288, 'Tell someone grieving the same loss that you are there if they ever want to talk.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 289, 'Write about what you would do together if you had one more ordinary afternoon.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 290, 'Choose one day a month to visit, call or remember them in a special way, if a regular ritual helps.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 291, 'Turn off notifications for an evening and let yourself have quiet.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 292, 'Write a letter from the person you lost to you, imagining what they might say.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 293, 'Spend a few minutes sitting with a plant, a tree or a view, and let your mind wander to them.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 294, 'Make a gentle plan for the first holiday without them, including a way to step away if you need to.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 295, 'Ask a friend to send you a message on their birthday, so you do not feel alone that day.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 296, 'Notice one small way you have cared for yourself this week, and thank yourself for it.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 297, 'Choose a meaningful place to scatter flowers, leave a stone or say a few words.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 298, 'Write down a piece of advice they once gave you, and how it has helped.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 299, 'Eat a piece of fruit or a handful of nuts in the middle of the afternoon.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 300, 'Tell a friend how they could mention the person you lost in conversation, if you would like them to.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 301, 'Rest in a quiet room for ten minutes without any screens.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 302, 'Make a small photo book or album of the person you lost, adding just a few pictures today.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 303, 'Talk with your manager about a flexible schedule for a while, if returning to work feels heavy.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 304, 'Look for a moment of beauty today, a sunset, a leaf or a kind face, and pause for it.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 305, 'Invite a child to draw a picture of a memory with the person who died.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 306, 'Write the person''s name in the sand, snow or dirt, or on a foggy window.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 307, 'Stand or sit by water, a lake, a fountain or even a running faucet, and let the sound settle you.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 308, 'Give yourself an extra layer of comfort tonight, like a heating pad, warm socks or a soft pillow.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 309, 'Ask yourself what you need most right now, rest, company, food or quiet, and give yourself one.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 310, 'Share one of their sayings with someone, and tell them where it came from.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 311, 'Notice whether you are avoiding a room or a place, and let that be okay for now.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 312, 'Go to a grief support group once, and simply listen if you do not want to speak.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 313, 'Write a short list of the ways they made the world kinder.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 314, 'Cook a simple dish they taught you, or one you made together.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 315, 'Pause before a big decision about their home or belongings, and give yourself more time if you can.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 316, 'Let a friend help you decide what to keep, give away or store, when you are ready.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 317, 'Spend a few minutes watching birds, squirrels or clouds from a window.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 318, 'Write down something you are looking forward to, even if it is only tomorrow''s coffee.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 319, 'Ask for an extra day off around an anniversary, if you are able.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 320, 'Hold a photo of them and tell them about something good that happened lately.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 321, 'Bring flowers to their resting place, or to a spot that reminds you of them.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 322, 'Remember that you can call or text 988, the Suicide and Crisis Lifeline, any time grief feels too heavy to carry alone or brings thoughts of not wanting to live.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 323, 'Go for a gentle walk in the rain or snow, dressed for it, and notice the quiet.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 324, 'Try out a new routine for the evenings that used to be shared, like a walk or a phone call with a friend.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 325, 'Make a gift in their memory for someone who loved them too.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 326, 'Tell a grieving friend one specific thing you can do for them this week.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 327, 'Notice whether your grief feels lighter, heavier or just different this season, and let it be what it is.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 328, 'Visit somewhere new and imagine telling them about it afterward.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 329, 'Write a list of songs, books and movies that remind you of them.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 330, 'Put on music you enjoy while you do a chore, and let it carry you through.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 331, 'Let yourself smile at a memory of them today.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 332, 'Take a few slow breaths before walking into a gathering where people may ask about your loss.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 333, 'Ask someone to help you mark a hard date with something comforting, like a meal or a walk.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 334, 'Keep a candle, photo or small object of theirs in one corner of your home as a quiet place to remember.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 335, 'Tell someone what has helped you most since the loss, so it might help them one day too.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 336, 'Write about how you have changed since they died, without needing it to sound good or bad.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 337, 'Share a meal with someone who also misses them, and set a place or say a toast for them.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 338, 'Let yourself enjoy a lazy morning in bed with a book or a warm drink.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 339, 'Notice your breathing as you wake up, and take three easy breaths before getting up.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 340, 'Choose a charity, garden or bench to dedicate in their name someday, and write down the idea.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 341, 'Listen to a song you both loved and let yourself sing along, even quietly.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 342, 'Find a quiet way to include them in a celebration, like a photo on the table or their favorite dish.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 343, 'Spend a few minutes tidying their photo or memory space so it feels cared for.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 344, 'Write a gentle note to yourself to read on the next hard day.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 345, 'Ask a trusted friend to sit with you while you watch a home video, if you want company for it.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 346, 'Go outdoors at dawn or dusk and watch the light for a few quiet minutes.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 347, 'Sort one more small item of theirs, only if today feels like the right day.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 348, 'Let a friend know that a gentle check-in text means a lot, even if you do not reply right away.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 349, 'Spend a little time on a hobby you used to enjoy, for just ten minutes.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 350, 'Notice a small kindness from a stranger or friend today, and take it in.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 351, 'Tell the person you lost, out loud or on paper, what this season has been like.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 352, 'Look back over this challenge and choose one gentle step you would like to keep doing.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 353, 'Make a plan for the next time grief hits in public: a breath, a quiet spot, a person to text.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 354, 'Let yourself go easy on chores this week, and do only what truly needs doing.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 355, 'Talk to someone about the person you lost who did not know them, and describe who they were.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 356, 'Keep a jar of small notes about them, adding one memory today.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 357, 'Ask a friend to take a walk with you on the anniversary or a birthday.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 358, 'Drink a warm glass of water or herbal tea before bed.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 359, 'Rest your hand on a pet, pillow or blanket, and notice the softness under your palm.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 360, 'Write a few lines about what love looks like now that they are gone.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 361, 'Notice the time of year, and name one memory of them tied to this exact season.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 362, 'Ask a counselor, faith leader or support group about what feels stuck, if you would like another person''s help.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 363, 'Spend a moment thanking your body for carrying you through these days.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 364, 'Choose one way to honor the person you lost this week, small and quiet, just for you.'),
  ('gentle-steps-after-a-loss', 365, 'Say their name once more, and let it be both a goodbye for today and a hello for tomorrow.'),
  ('learning-something-new', 1, 'Write down three things you have always been curious about learning, then circle the one that makes you smile.'),
  ('learning-something-new', 2, 'Pick one skill to explore for this challenge and say it out loud, so it feels real.'),
  ('learning-something-new', 3, 'Set a timer for ten minutes and spend it on your new skill, then stop when it rings, even mid-task.'),
  ('learning-something-new', 4, 'Let yourself be a beginner on purpose today: try something you will do badly and notice that you are still fine.'),
  ('learning-something-new', 5, 'Ask someone who knows your chosen skill for one tip, and write it down word for word.'),
  ('learning-something-new', 6, 'Visit your local library and borrow one beginner book on the thing you want to learn.'),
  ('learning-something-new', 7, 'Watch one free beginner lesson on your topic, and pause it to try each step yourself.'),
  ('learning-something-new', 8, 'Explain one thing you learned this week to a friend or family member in two minutes or less.'),
  ('learning-something-new', 9, 'Notice one small thing that feels easier than when you started, and name it out loud.'),
  ('learning-something-new', 10, 'Choose a regular time for practice, such as after breakfast or before dinner, and put it on your calendar.'),
  ('learning-something-new', 11, 'Write one question about your topic that you genuinely want answered, and tape it where you will see it.'),
  ('learning-something-new', 12, 'Look up a word you heard recently but never quite understood, and use it in a sentence today.'),
  ('learning-something-new', 13, 'Ask a child to teach you something they know well, like a game, a drawing trick or a dance move.'),
  ('learning-something-new', 14, 'Make a mistake while practicing, then write one sentence about what it showed you.'),
  ('learning-something-new', 15, 'Start a small learning log in a notebook: the date, what you tried and one thing you noticed.'),
  ('learning-something-new', 16, 'Take your practice outside for ten minutes, even if it is just reading notes on a porch or bench.'),
  ('learning-something-new', 17, 'Try one new recipe that uses a technique you have never done before, like folding dough or poaching an egg.'),
  ('learning-something-new', 18, 'Celebrate the effort you put in today with something small, like a favorite song or a cup of tea.'),
  ('learning-something-new', 19, 'Gather the simple tools or materials you need for your skill and set them in one easy spot.'),
  ('learning-something-new', 20, 'Learn how to say hello and thank you in a language you have never studied.'),
  ('learning-something-new', 21, 'Sketch a coffee mug from life for five minutes, focusing on its shape rather than making it perfect.'),
  ('learning-something-new', 22, 'Find out what the first lesson usually covers for your skill, and do just that first lesson.'),
  ('learning-something-new', 23, 'Tell one person what you are learning, so it becomes something you share rather than a secret.'),
  ('learning-something-new', 24, 'Read one page about your topic slowly, and underline the sentence that surprised you most.'),
  ('learning-something-new', 25, 'Ask an older relative about a skill they learned when they were young, and listen to the whole story.'),
  ('learning-something-new', 26, 'Practice the same small thing three times in a row, and notice what changes between tries.'),
  ('learning-something-new', 27, 'Look up a place on a map that you know nothing about, and read one paragraph about it.'),
  ('learning-something-new', 28, 'Try a new walking route to a familiar spot and notice three things you never saw before.'),
  ('learning-something-new', 29, 'Write a sentence that begins, "I am curious about…" and finish it as many ways as you can in two minutes.'),
  ('learning-something-new', 30, 'Learn the name of one tree or plant you pass often, and say its name when you walk by.'),
  ('learning-something-new', 31, 'Look for a free community class or workshop nearby and write down the date of one you could attend.'),
  ('learning-something-new', 32, 'Invite a friend to learn something small with you this week, even over a video call.'),
  ('learning-something-new', 33, 'Spend ten minutes practicing before checking your phone in the morning.'),
  ('learning-something-new', 34, 'Find the smallest possible version of your skill, like one chord, one stitch or one phrase, and work on only that.'),
  ('learning-something-new', 35, 'Draw a quick map of what you want to learn, with the basics in the middle and the fun extras around them.'),
  ('learning-something-new', 36, 'Notice a moment of frustration while learning, take three slow breaths and then try once more.'),
  ('learning-something-new', 37, 'Try a tiny taste of knitting: cast on ten stitches with any yarn and needles you can find or borrow.'),
  ('learning-something-new', 38, 'Watch someone skilled at your topic, in person or on video, and notice one thing they do with ease.'),
  ('learning-something-new', 39, 'Write down one thing you understand now that you did not understand when you started.'),
  ('learning-something-new', 40, 'Practice in a new spot at home today, like the kitchen table or a sunny corner, and see how it feels.'),
  ('learning-something-new', 41, 'Read about the history of your skill for ten minutes and note one surprising fact.'),
  ('learning-something-new', 42, 'Teach a pet, a plant or an empty chair what you learned today, saying it out loud as if to a student.'),
  ('learning-something-new', 43, 'Make a short list of words that belong to your new skill, and learn what two of them mean.'),
  ('learning-something-new', 44, 'Repeat a short exercise from earlier in this challenge and notice how it feels this time.'),
  ('learning-something-new', 45, 'Pick one beginner mistake you keep making and slow down enough to catch it once today.'),
  ('learning-something-new', 46, 'Look out the window and learn one fact about the weather or season you see, like why leaves change color.'),
  ('learning-something-new', 47, 'Try a tiny taste of drawing: copy a simple leaf, noticing where its veins branch.'),
  ('learning-something-new', 48, 'Write down one way your new skill could someday bring joy to someone else.'),
  ('learning-something-new', 49, 'Practice for ten minutes in the evening, then write one line in your log before bed.'),
  ('learning-something-new', 50, 'Ask a librarian to recommend a book or resource for a complete beginner in your topic.'),
  ('learning-something-new', 51, 'Learn one new fact about a bird you see or hear around your home.'),
  ('learning-something-new', 52, 'Allow your practice to be messy today and resist the urge to start over when it looks imperfect.'),
  ('learning-something-new', 53, 'Tell someone about a mistake you made while learning, and laugh about it together if you can.'),
  ('learning-something-new', 54, 'Find a free online lecture or talk about a topic you know nothing about, and listen to the first ten minutes.'),
  ('learning-something-new', 55, 'Try a tiny taste of a new language by labeling five things in your kitchen with sticky notes.'),
  ('learning-something-new', 56, 'Write a short thank-you note to someone who once taught you something, even if you never send it.'),
  ('learning-something-new', 57, 'Break your skill into three small parts and pick one part to work on this week.'),
  ('learning-something-new', 58, 'Practice with your nondominant hand for two minutes, just to feel what being new is like.'),
